Take a batch of $1000$ items. Line A makes $500$, line B makes $300$, and line C makes $200$.

The defective items are $0.01 \cdot 500 = 5$ from line A, $0.04 \cdot 300 = 12$ from line B, and $0.09 \cdot 200 = 18$ from line C. In total $5 + 12 + 18 = 35$ items are defective.

P(C \mid \text{defective}) = \frac{18}{35}
